  "narrative": "I reassessed the due validation for H18. The estimate is already signed to the hypothesis direction, so the discovery signed estimate of about +0.796 and validation signed estimate of about +0.781 both support the registered direction: KEAP1-loss cells have a less negative NFE2L2 dependency score, i.e. weaker NFE2L2 dependency. The independent validation interval is multiplicity-aware and remains entirely positive, approximately +0.752 to +0.809. Using the absolute overall NFE2L2 mean of about 0.093 as the baseline scale, the 10% clinical-significance threshold is about 0.0093; the validation effect is far above that threshold. Therefore the overall H18 association is well supported in this supplied dataset and I close the original overall investigation. This result also reinforces rejection of the original H5 direction: the data do not support KEAP1 loss causing stronger NFE2L2 dependency; instead the opposite association is supported. The earlier specificity audits did not show a strong batch_a, adenocarcinoma, or STK11-loss interaction, and STK11 loss alone was null-like for NFE2L2, so the validation now makes this one of the two strongest validated in-dataset findings, alongside validated TP53-loss/USP7. These remain associations within the supplied dataset, not causal statements or claims about external generalizability. Next, I propose two conditional KEAP1-loss analyses: within TP53-loss cells and within STK11-loss cells, to test whether the very large KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association persists in important co-alteration contexts. I also propose a WRN-by-adenocarcinoma interaction to test whether MSI-high/WRN dependency is lineage-subtype-specific. If future analyses do not undermine the major accepted effects, the next validation priority should be one of the strongest unvalidated accepted overall associations, preferably SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 or MSI-high/WRN.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence state after H18 validation: validated accepted overall effects are H12 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency and H18 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. H5 original KEAP1 direction remains rejected/closed; its validation evidence supports the reversed H18 association. Unvalidated accepted overall/context effects: H7 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H13 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency, H24 WRN adenocarcinoma subgroup, H25 USP7 adenocarcinoma subgroup, H34 SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 specificity in ARID1A-intact cells, H35 reversed batch_a attenuation interaction. Negative/closed overall findings remain BRAF mutation/BRAF dependency, ERBB2 amplification/ERBB2 dependency, overall ARID1A-loss/SMARCA2 dependency, MYC-amplification/POLR2A dependency, RB1-loss/KIF18A dependency, STK11-loss/NFE2L2 dependency, ARID1A-loss/SMARCA2 in SMARCA4-intact cells, and H29 original batch_a interaction direction. Unresolved borderline effects: H1/H19 KRAS mutation/KRAS dependency and H3/H20 EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency; H6 TP53 loss/MDM2 dependency. Next analyze priority can include H36 batch_a SMARCA4 mean effect, H31 KRAS lineage interaction, H32 MDM2 lineage interaction, H21 MDM2 adenocarcinoma, H22 SMARCA4-by-ARID1A interaction, H10/H11 MYC effects, H15/H16/H17 broad cross-talk hypotheses, and newly proposed KEAP1 TP53-loss/STK11-loss conditional effects plus WRN lineage interaction. Validation priority: after upcoming discovery results, request independent validation for H7 or H13 unless new evidence strongly changes priorities. Validation budget remains 8 new requests. Keep interpreting signed estimates only and keep claims limited to supplied-dataset associations."
